From 1c9678c88ecf2043e915efe81efefac4d91b94b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:08:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/49] R5: index-load workers follow the backend's
 connections, as in stock

The worker count was min(connections+GOMAXPROCS, max(2, GOMAXPROCS)): on a
machine with one or two CPUs two index files were downloaded at a time
whatever the backend allowed (stock: all 5 connections of S3 or REST), and
with four CPUs four instead of five.

Now max(connections+min(GOMAXPROCS, 2), GOMAXPROCS): on one and two CPUs
this is stock's connections+GOMAXPROCS; everywhere all connections can
download while up to two index files are decoded; the count is never above
stock's. Two connections on four CPUs (the local backend) keep four workers.

The league's TestIndexLoadAdmissionAndCancellation asserted the removed cap
(at most max(2, GOMAXPROCS) loads with 32 connections); its bound is now the
worker count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
